  "id": "COMPOUND:17827 - PROTEIN:6304",
  "verbalization": "Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate is implicated in the regulation of Microtubule-associated protein 1B through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple molecules, including Thioredoxin, which in turn is targeted by Pseudopterosin Q and Tenuifolin E. These intermediates are all known to interact with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, indicating a potential pathway where Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate may influence the protein through its interaction with Thioredoxin. The consistent presence of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a target across different pathways underscores a possible role in cellular processes involving microtubules. The integration of these findings highlights a possible mechanism where Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate modulates the activity of Thioredoxin, which then affects Microtubule-associated protein 1B, suggesting a broader regulatory network. The evidence supports a link between the compound and the protein, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
